yunohost (12.1.41.77) stable; urgency=low

  * Runtime instances: wire every XDG location to the per-instance state
    directory, not just the config path. OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR only overrides
    an app's Path.config; project/repo storage is derived from XDG_DATA_HOME
    instead (falling back to $HOME only if unset), so a mis-set config-only
    override could let every user's instance resolve its data/cache/state to
    the same shared fallback. Adds cache_dir_env/state_dir_env alongside the
    existing home_env/config_dir_env/data_dir_env fields and maps all five
    to the instance's own StateDirectory.

 -- NostrHost <nostrhost@example.com>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:05:00 +0000

yunohost (12.1.41.76) stable; urgency=low

  * Nostr network defaults: applying changes no longer loses added relays or
    storage servers. The connectivity config is now persisted before the
    catalogue/nsite projection side-effects, and the catalogue synchroniser
    restart is queued with `systemctl --no-block` instead of running
    synchronously (a slow-stopping unit could previously stall the apply
    before the config was written, so added defaults did not survive).
    - The admin "Nostr network" page also reports a failed apply instead of
      claiming the defaults were updated.

